<SiteLayout
  title="About — Shubham Kumar"
  description="A little about me: writing code, solving problems, music, physics, and the things I’m interested in."
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <h1>About me.</h1>
    <p>
      I’m Shubham. I like solving problems and understanding how things work.
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I spend a lot of time writing code. I enjoy it, but the part I like most
      is working out how to solve a problem. Software is where I’ve had the most
      practice. In most other things, I’m happy to be learning.
    </p>
    <p>
      Physics, astronomy, maths, computers—I’m interested in all of them, and in
      the things that connect them. I don’t really have favourites. Almost
      anything becomes interesting once you look at it closely enough.
    </p>
    <p>
      I’d probably call myself a jack of all trades. “Interest trumps
      experience” sums up how I feel about that. Not knowing much about
      something doesn’t put me off wanting to understand it.
    </p>
    <h2 id="music">Away from code</h2>
    <p>
      I like riding my bike and listening to music. My taste in music is fairly
      broad, but I’m especially drawn to good lyrics. There’s something
      beautiful about expressing a complicated feeling in just a few words.
    </p>
    <p>
      I write as well. The subjects vary: national anthems, the stories we tell
      ourselves, space, a letter from Feynman to his wife. My{" "}
      <a href="/writings">essays</a> are probably a better introduction to that
      side of me than a list of interests.
    </p>
    <p>
      My favourite painter is Leonardo da Vinci. I admire his art, but also the
      fact that he was good at so many other things. That breadth of interest is
      a big part of why I like him.
    </p>
    <p>
      As for things that get on my nerves: a lack of common sense. I wish it
      were a little more common.
    </p>
    <section id="feynman" class="feynman-note">
      <h2>Feynman says this well</h2>
      <p>
        There’s a passage about a flower that captures something I believe. You
        can appreciate how beautiful it is and want to understand the cells, the
        colours, and the processes behind it. Learning about one doesn’t take
        away from the other.
      </p>
      <p>
        That’s how I feel about a lot of things. Understanding them gives me
        more to enjoy.
      </p>
      <details>
        <summary>
          Read the passage <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <FeynmanStory />
      </details>
    </section>
